The `load_http_source` uses `?` on `read_content`, which means if it fails (due to a race condition), it will propagate the error upward. Looking at how `RemoteLoader::new()` handles errors from `load_http_source`:

```rust
match result {
    Ok(loaded) => { ... }
    Err(e) => {
        tracing::warn!("Failed to load templates from {}: {}", source.url, e);
    }
}
```

So if `read_content` returns an error, it logs a warning and moves on. This would cause the source to not load from cache, and since it doesn't retry fetching, it would skip the source entirely for this run.


I should modify `load_http_source` to catch race condition errors from `read_content` and fall back to fetching from the remote source instead of propagating the error.

